<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48107" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">thēca</span></b> , ae, f.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θήκη,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that in which any
				thing is enclosed</i>, <i>an envelope</i>, <i>hull</i>, <i>cover</i>, <i>case</i>, <i>sheath</i>, etc. (syn.
			vagina): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">grani,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 48, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">efferri sine thecis vasa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 4, 23, § 52</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Att. 4, 7, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 6,
				3, 61</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">calamaria,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Claud. 35</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Mart. 14, 19, 1</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Amm. 28, 4, 13</span></i>.</div>
